@nakedible, why did you decide to go with:

```rs
pub struct Time<T> { ... }
pub struct Fixed;

fn system(time: Res<Time<Fixed>>) {}
```

as opposed to this?:

```rs
pub struct Time {...}

#[derive(Deref, DerefMut)]
pub struct FixedTime(Time);

fn system(time: Res<FixedTime>) {}
```

I.e. why `Time` wraps specialization struct, and not the other way around?

> Can you give an advice on how I can create a custom `Time` specialization?
>
> In my own crate, I can't add `impl Time<MyTime> {}`, because [of the orphan rule].

It's a little clunky, but ~~you could implement the specialized methods using a trait.~~ (edit: didn't see you had already considered that) yeah, I think a custom trait is the way to do it.

```rust
pub trait MyTrait {
    /* ... */
}

impl MyTrait for Time<MyTime> {
    /* ... */
}
```

